<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  launchd job for the ask lane, in the USER domain (a LaunchAgent).

  WHY AN AGENT, WHEN THE SCAN RUNS AS A DAEMON. The scan worker is a
  LaunchDaemon on purpose: it starts at boot with nobody logged in, which is the
  only way "always on" is true (see com.eternalgy.gmapworker.daemon.plist). The
  ask lane cannot follow it. ego lite will not start without a GUI session, and
  the agy on this machine was signed in interactively and keeps its Google
  session in the login keychain — a process in the system domain has neither, so
  both engines would find themselves signed out in the one context where nobody
  is watching the log.

  THE PRICE, AND THE SETTING THAT PAYS IT. An agent starts at login, not at boot.
  A mini that reboots at 3am and stops at the login window runs no agent, and the
  failure is invisible — chatgpt@mini simply stops being listed and bare calls
  fall back to the container. So this file is only half the install: Automatic
  login must be on (System Settings -> Users & Groups -> Automatic login), and
  FileVault must stay off for it to work at all.

  Install it with the sed line in README.md — launchd does not expand ~, so
  __HOME__, __NODE__ and __NODEBIN__ must be real paths before this file is loaded.

  WORKER_TYPES pins this process to one lane rather than letting macmini.mjs
  build its default two, and it is set HERE rather than left to
  ~/.gmap-worker.env on purpose: that file carries WORKER_TYPES=ping,gmap.scan as
  the default for the unpinned scan daemon, and process.loadEnvFile does not
  override a variable already present in the environment. This line is what keeps
  the two lanes from collapsing onto each other.

  PATH carries the nvm bin directory because `opencode` (the muse engine) is
  installed beside node there, and ~/.local/bin because ego-browser and agy are
  installed there. A launchd job inherits neither.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.eternalgy.gmapworker.ask</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__NODE__</string>
    <string>__HOME__/automation-tools/worker/macmini.mjs</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__HOME__/automation-tools</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>10</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/gmap-worker-ask.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/gmap-worker-ask.log</string>

  <!--
    No LAB_TOKEN here. macmini.mjs reads it from ~/.gmap-worker.env at chmod 600,
    for the same reason the daemon does: a plist is readable by every process on
    the box and that token is a root shell on the lab container.
  -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>__NODEBIN__:__HOME__/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>__HOME__</string>
    <key>WORKER_NAME</key>
    <string>macmini-ask</string>
    <key>WORKER_TYPES</key>
    <string>chatgpt.ask,chatgpt.probe,meta.ask,meta.probe,muse.ask,muse.probe,agy.ask,agy.probe</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
